@page "/docs"
@attribute [FollowsModeSwitch]
@inject Registry Registry
@inject ApiMetadata Api

@*
    The front door to the docs: what IzzyBlazor is, a first look at the code, one live example
    under the page's mode switch, how it's built, what's in the box (from components.json), what it
    needs, and where else to look. The sidebar covers the docs sections, so this page doesn't
    repeat them as cards.
*@

<PageTitle>Docs · IzzyBlazor</PageTitle>
<HeadContent><meta name="description" content="IzzyBlazor's documentation: SSR-first Blazor components, how they work in each render mode, what's in the library and how to start." /></HeadContent>

<article class="site-article">
    <Stack Gap="3" Class="site-pagehead">
        <Heading Level="1" Size="TextSize.Xl3">Documentation</Heading>
        <TextBlock Size="TextSize.Lg" Color="Color.Muted">
            IzzyBlazor is a Blazor component library built for static SSR. Pages arrive as real HTML, a small script brings
            them to life without a circuit, and the same markup binds to C# on the pages you make interactive.
        </TextBlock>
    </Stack>

    <Row Gap="2" Align="Align.Center" Class="site-install">
        <TextBlock As="span" Color="Color.Muted" aria-hidden="true">$</TextBlock>
        <Code>@Install</Code>
        <CopyButton Text="@Install" Label="Copy the install command" Size="ControlSize.Sm" />
    </Row>
    <TextBlock>One set of components for every page. This form posts and validates on a static page, with JavaScript off too, and runs over a circuit on an interactive one, with no change to the markup. The model takes the post through <Code>[SupplyParameterFromForm]</Code>:</TextBlock>
    <Code Block Language="razor">@FirstLook</Code>
    <Row Gap="3" Wrap>
        <Button Href="docs/get-started">Get started</Button>
        <Button Href="docs/components" Variant="ButtonVariant.Outline" Accent="Accent.Neutral">Browse components</Button>
    </Row>

    <Heading Level="2">Off · Static · Live</Heading>
    <TextBlock>Examples on this site run three ways. Pick one with the switch, here and on component pages:</TextBlock>
    <List Gap="2">
        <ListItem><strong>Off</strong>: JavaScript disabled, so you see exactly what the HTML and CSS do on their own.</ListItem>
        <ListItem><strong>Static</strong>: a static SSR page with IzzyBlazor's script, which adds keyboard handling, live values and the like. No circuit.</ListItem>
        <ListItem><strong>Live</strong>: an interactive page on Blazor Server, where C# event handlers and <Code>@@bind</Code> run.</ListItem>
    </List>
    <ExampleViewer Example="home-settings" ModeSwitch />

    <Heading Level="2">How it's built</Heading>
    <Grid Columns="new() { Base = 1, Md = 2 }" Gap="6" Class="site-concepts">
        <Stack Gap="1">
            <Heading Level="3" Size="TextSize.Md" Outline="false" Class="site-concept-title">One set for every render mode</Heading>
            <TextBlock Color="Color.Muted">The same components on static, Server, WebAssembly and Auto pages. Nearly all work with JavaScript off and do more with it. <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">Render modes</Anchor></TextBlock>
        </Stack>
        <Stack Gap="1">
            <Heading Level="3" Size="TextSize.Md" Outline="false" Class="site-concept-title">Forms that post</Heading>
            <TextBlock Color="Color.Muted"><Code>Form</Code> and its fields bind on a static post and on an interactive page, with labels, limits and messages from your model's attributes. <Anchor Href="docs/common/forms">Forms and validation</Anchor></TextBlock>
        </Stack>
        <Stack Gap="1">
            <Heading Level="3" Size="TextSize.Md" Outline="false" Class="site-concept-title">State in the URL</Heading>
            <TextBlock Color="Color.Muted">Table, FilterForm and Pagination keep sorting, filters and the page in the query string, so they work with no circuit and links keep them. <Anchor Href="docs/components/table">Table</Anchor></TextBlock>
        </Stack>
        <Stack Gap="1">
            <Heading Level="3" Size="TextSize.Md" Outline="false" Class="site-concept-title">Style props and themes</Heading>
            <TextBlock Color="Color.Muted">Spacing, sizes and colors as parameters, and <Code>IzzyTheme</Code> for the preset, brand and fonts, rendered on the server so the theme is there on first paint. <Anchor Href="docs/common/style-props">Style props</Anchor> · <Anchor Href="docs/theming/themes">Theming</Anchor></TextBlock>
        </Stack>
        <Stack Gap="1">
            <Heading Level="3" Size="TextSize.Md" Outline="false" Class="site-concept-title">Native elements first</Heading>
            <TextBlock Color="Color.Muted">Buttons, dialogs, selects and disclosures are the browser's own, so focus, keyboard and screen readers work as the platform defines them; the script adds ARIA where it adds behavior.</TextBlock>
        </Stack>
    </Grid>

    <Heading Level="2">What's in the box</Heading>
    <TextBlock>@Registry.ComponentCountLabel components in @Registry.Categories.Count categories. <Anchor Href="docs/components">See them all</Anchor>.</TextBlock>
    <Grid Columns="new() { Base = 1, Sm = 2, Lg = 3 }" Gap="3" Class="site-box">
        @foreach (var category in Registry.Categories)
        {
            var components = Registry.InCategory(category).ToList();
            <div class="site-box-category">
                <Heading Level="3" Size="TextSize.Md" Outline="false" Class="site-box-title">
                    <Anchor Href="@($"docs/components#{ApiMetadata.Anchor(category).Replace(' ', '-')}")" Underline="AnchorUnderline.Hover">@category</Anchor>
                    <span class="site-box-count">@components.Count<span class="ib-visually-hidden"> components</span></span>
                </Heading>
                <TextBlock Size="TextSize.Sm" Color="Color.Muted">
                    @for (var i = 0; i < Math.Min(4, components.Count); i++)
                    {
                        var component = components[i];
                        @(i == 0 ? "" : ", ")<Anchor Href="@Registry.OverviewHref(component)" Underline="AnchorUnderline.Hover">@component.Name</Anchor>
                    }
                    @if (components.Count > 4)
                    {
                        @($" and {components.Count - 4} more")
                    }
                </TextBlock>
            </div>
        }
    </Grid>

    <Heading Level="2">Requirements</Heading>
    <List Gap="2">
        <ListItem><strong>.NET 10</strong>, in a Blazor Web App: static pages, and Server, WebAssembly or Auto pages.</ListItem>
        <ListItem><strong>Two packages</strong>: <Code>IzzyBlazor</Code> for the server project, and <Code>IzzyBlazor.Core</Code> for a <Code>.Client</Code> project. <Anchor Href="docs/get-started/webassembly-and-auto#packages">Packages</Anchor></ListItem>
        <ListItem><strong>Current browsers</strong>: Chrome and Edge 123+, Firefox 128+, Safari 17.5+. Newer features, such as the customizable select, are used where the browser has them.</ListItem>
        <ListItem><strong>MIT licensed</strong>. Pro components are planned.</ListItem>
    </List>

    <Heading Level="2">Resources</Heading>
    <List Gap="2">
        <ListItem><Anchor Href="demos">Demos</Anchor>: realistic scenarios in all three modes, with the source.</ListItem>
        <ListItem><Anchor Href="https://github.com/enabledevmode/izzyblazor">GitHub</Anchor>: the source and issues.</ListItem>
        <ListItem><Anchor Href="https://github.com/enabledevmode/izzyblazor/releases">Release notes</Anchor>: what changed in each version.</ListItem>
        <ListItem><Anchor Href="izzyblazor.api.json">API metadata</Anchor>: every component's API as JSON, for tools and AI assistants.</ListItem>
    </List>
</article>

@code {
    private const string Install = "dotnet add package IzzyBlazor --prerelease";

    private const string FirstLook = """
        <Form Model="Signup" FormName="signup" OnValidSubmit="SaveAsync">
            <TextField @bind-Value="Signup.Email" />
            <Button Submit>Sign up</Button>
        </Form>

        @code {
            [SupplyParameterFromForm(FormName = "signup")]
            private SignupModel? Signup { get; set; }

            protected override void OnInitialized() => Signup ??= new();
        }
        """;
}
